":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"wrT5DbuM24B9ExBdSSz2_g","review_id":"YPLYelyLSpUmfsDpMwKzjw","date":"2017-04-29T17:45:08","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9405721426010132,"text_excerpt":"Cool place to get gelato, and/or a coffee and I guess they serve breakfast as well. I ordered the pecan praline gelato for dinner one evening as it was too hot to eat a whole meal. I had to eat it fast-luckily it was only one scoop because it is so incredibly hot all day and all night in New Orleans! (I am surprised there are not more crabby people here due to the irritability of the heat-hahah!). There was a small patio outside with chairs and tables to eat which was nice. Local artist paintings were inside to purchase was nice."},{"business_id":"wrT5DbuM24B9ExBdSSz2_g","review_id":"tXJ58QuSS_yq1kDDnlb90g","date":"2016-11-11T19:40:03","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9339475631713867,"text_excerpt":"Great gelato spot in the French quarter. It's a nice cool down spot with a lovely outdoor alley patio. Make sure to check the consistency of your chosen flavors prior to ordering as their freezer definitely needs a tune up. We ordered dark chocolate, coconut (their signature), sweet cream, and creme freche. All of the flavors were very good. In my humble opinion, the creme freche is a must order! The server was an older gentlemen and gruff but somehow added to the experience. The line was out the door but worth the wait. If I was a local, I'd be a regular here!"},{"business_id":"wrT5DbuM24B9ExBdSSz2_g","review_id":"i_Xig5dWi1ILj5l9e888lg","date":"2011-07-11T18:42:59","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9311286211013794,"text_excerpt":"In New Orleans, being the hot and muggy hot sauna that it is, I was super happy whenever we could go inside an AC'd place. I got even happier if it consisted of a ice cold treat for me. La Divina had really good flavors of gelato. It was a bit pricey (over $4 for the small), but I guess all gelato/froyo is getting to be expensive these days. And this place being in a touristy area, it makes sense. We chose the Mexican chocolate + English tea and biscuits flavors. I loved the biscuit pieces~ It brought texture to the gelato."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"wrT5DbuM24B9ExBdSSz2_g","photo_id":"fAxkC8RmAGGnPnRrtkKsyg","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/fAxkC8RmAGGnPnRrtkKsyg.jpg","visual_representativeness":1.0}]},"notebook_case":null}
